    key: 'ipns-record-selection',
    effort: 'high',
    prompt: `Find the IPNS record creation/validation code: createIpnsRecord and marshalIpnsRecord in @cipherbox/core (search packages/core/src for "ipns"), and any IPNS validator / selector / Compare logic (it may live in the "ipns" npm package the code imports under node_modules, and the authoritative rule is the IPNS spec / go-ipns).
CLAIM TO TEST (confirm BOTH halves):
(1) Across competing valid records for the SAME name, the record with the HIGHER sequence number always wins.
(2) On EQUAL sequence numbers, the record with the LATER validity / EOL (expiry) wins.
This decides (a) whether a republish that re-signs the SAME sequence number with a fresh/later EOL is preferred over the prior copy (validity refresh WITHOUT a sequence bump), and (b) whether a forward-sequence record always beats any lower-sequence record regardless of EOL.
