  },
  {
    key: 'no-generation-on-resolve',
    effort: 'medium',
    prompt: `Search the resolve/verify paths:
- apps/api/src/ipns/ipns.service.ts resolveRecord
- packages/sdk-core/src/ipns/index.ts (resolve function)
- crates/api-client/src/ipns.rs (resolve_ipns_verified / VerifiedResolve struct and its verification)
CLAIM TO TEST: NO resolve or verify path checks any per-node "generation" field or any rollback high-water mark BEYOND the raw IPNS sequence number plus signature/name-derivation/value-to-cid verification. I.e. there is currently no generation-based anti-rollback anywhere on resolve.
For each path, list exactly WHAT it verifies (signature? name derivation? value==cid? sequence?) and confirm the ABSENCE of any generation check. Cite lines.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'cas-gate-publish-only',
    effort: 'medium',
    prompt: `Read apps/api/src/ipns/ipns.service.ts.
CLAIM TO TEST: the forward-only sequence CAS / anti-rollback gate (around lines 295-317 — the check that rejects a publish whose sequence is not strictly greater than the stored sequence) is enforced ONLY on the publish() path. resolveRecord does NOT re-apply this gate to a network record before returning it — so a network record at a sequence HIGHER than the DB's stored sequence is served to the client even though it never passed the CAS gate.
Confirm (or refute) and cite the gate's location and the absence of an equivalent check in resolveRecord.`,
